<title>LITHUANIA: U.S. CEME to buy Lithuania TV stake-report.</title>
<headline>U.S. CEME to buy Lithuania TV stake-report.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-based Central European Media Enterprises (CEME) is to buy a 40 percent stake in private Lithuanian television station, LNK, newspaper Lietuvos rytas said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted the state-owned Agricultural Bank as saying that it had sold its stake in LNK to CEME for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>It said that the venture in Lithuania was the first for CEME in the Baltic states, although it already has a stake in Czech channel Nova and projects in Germany and Slovenia.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
